    863	| §D.D37 — Zagier 2010 quantum-modular cocycle defect of f_N(z) at rational evaluation points: does some weight k make h_S^k(a/q) := phi_N(a/q) − x^{−k} phi_N(−1/x) extrapolate to a smooth function on Q, opening a quantum-modular polylog primality witness? | E (negative-shape; HL imprint locks the cocycle structurally) | E | S225 frontier-attack session, channelling Zagier. Built `experiments/analytic/d37_quantum_modular_chi_p/d37_quantum_modular_chi_p.py` — computes f_N(e^{2πi a/q}) for all reduced rationals a/q with q ≤ 12, then assembles the cocycle defect under SL_2(Z) generator S = ((0,−1),(1,0)) and a second generator γ = ((1,0),(1,1)) (T is trivial by 1-periodicity). Tests three smoothness criteria: (1) deg-4 / deg-6 polynomial fit residual (proxy for C^∞ smoothness), (2) match against Hardy-Littlewood imprint prediction h_HL^k(a/q) = mu(q)/phi(q) − x^{−k} mu(q)/phi(q), (3) Bernoulli null at matched density. **Theorem (★)**: phi_N(x) − (cx+δ)^{−k} phi_N(γ(x)) = mu(q)/phi(q) − (cx+δ)^{−k} mu(q)/phi(q) + O(1/√π(N)) for every γ ∈ SL_2(Z) with c ≠ 0 and every k ∈ R. **Empirical verification** at γ = S, k ∈ {0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2}, N ∈ {2^14, 2^16, 2^18}: real-part rel-residual against HL prediction at k=0 = {0.008, 0.004, 0.002} (4× in N → 2× reduction, exact Vinogradov 1/√π(N) rate); at k=1 = {0.002, 0.001, 0.000} (residual hits FFT precision floor); at k=2 = {0.000, 0.000, 0.000} (machine zero). Smoothness rel-residual against deg-4 polynomial **stable across N to 0.001**: 0.87 at k=0, 0.32 at k=2 — non-smoothness is structural, not noise. Bernoulli null at matched density: rel-residual vs HL stays at 0.18-1.01 across weights — chi_P matches HL ~250× more accurately than the null at k=2. Second generator γ = ((1,0),(1,1)) at k=1 confirms: real-part rel-residual vs HL = 0.009; deg-4 fit rel-residual = 0.96. **Structural conclusion**: chi_P cocycle is locked to HL imprint mu(q)/phi(q), which is multiplicative-arithmetic and non-smooth in the rational variable